# `$2` in an operand that `and` never evaluates still makes a two-argument
# lambda, which accepts two arguments and returns the short-circuited value.
#= {result: [false, false], inputs: {never: false}}
def {never} = import('inputs')
def constant = $(false and $2)
def runtime = $(never and $2)
[constant(1, 2), runtime(1, 2)]
